    "final_text": "I built the parser and serializer with no dependencies: `src/csv.js` exports `parse`, `stringify` and `CsvError`. The 6 tests in `test/csv.test.js` pass with `npm test`. I haven't committed anything.\n\n- **Round trip:** the tests cover `parse(stringify(rows))` with and without `skipEmptyLines`, and with a custom delimiter. The rows include `['']`, empty fields, embedded line breaks and quotes.\n- **BOM quoting (beyond the spec):** `stringify` quotes the first field of the output if it begins with a BOM. Without that, `parse` would strip the BOM and the round trip would fail. Other fields that start with a BOM are not quoted.\n- **`__proto__` headers:** in header mode, a column named `__proto__` becomes an ordinary key on the record object. It does not change the object's prototype.\n- **Test script:** `package.json` runs `node --test test/*.test.js`. Pointing `node --test` at the `test/` directory itself failed on this Node version, so I used the glob.",
